This builds the list's mail hub on trunk, one behavior per patch. Each
patch carries the spec text, README, and code for its step, so after
every patch the jail does what its spec.org and README.org say.

  client --SMTP--> OpenSMTPD --LMTP--> Dovecot --> INBOX
  Dovecot <--IMAP--> mbsync <--IMAPS--> Fastmail
    (INBOX, Next, Later, and Archive only)

1. The list moves to INBOX of its own Fastmail account, and the lists
   folder and its Fastmail rule go.
2. Dovecot becomes the only writer of the list. mbsync fetches into it
   over IMAP, as a login with a password.
3. The fetch becomes a two-way sync of INBOX and Archive.
4. Pat's login may archive and delete.
5. README.org documents the one-time import of the jj maildir.
6. OpenSMTPD replaces smtprelay, and hands posts straight to Dovecot
   over LMTP.
7. lab@lists.p7x.dev and freebsd-ports@lists.p7x.dev join the list's
   addresses.
8. Next and Later sync beside INBOX and Archive.

Patches 2 and 6 are the large ones, and neither splits further.
Patch 2 changes who owns the maildir, and the fetch, the ACL, the
passdbs, and the check all change with it. Any one of them alone
leaves a jail that cannot fetch. Patch 6 swaps one SMTP server for
another on the same port, and the two cannot both run.

Before deploying: delete the Fastmail rule that files list mail into
lists, empty the maildir and mbsync's state as README.org says, and
create Next and Later on Fastmail.

I applied the series with git am onto trunk, and each libexec script
passes sh -n at every patch. Dovecot, smtpd, and the jail build are
not installed here, so no step was run on a jail. That the ACL's k
right lets mbsync create a top-level mailbox under acl_globals_only
is still untested.

Changes in v13:
- Each spec change is in the patch whose code it describes, as you
  asked [1]. v12's four spec-only patches are gone. Their text is
  spread across the patches above, and their two corrections, what
  Dovecot does to a reader's write and the header check left to
  OpenSMTPD, are in patches 2 and 6.
- Patch 1 is new. It splits the move to INBOX out of "Let Dovecot
  write the list".
- The spec covers only what this series builds, and is 398 lines
  where v12's was 506. v12 also specced the clients: Pat's notmuch and
  Emacs on beastie, folder tags, git send-email, and retiring the mail
  bookmark. None of that has code here, so it is left out, to come
  with the series that builds the clients. The spec's out of scope
  says so.
- lab-claude's client keeps working at each step. It pulls INBOX
  instead of lists from patch 1, and its README.org describes what
  lab-mail takes from patch 6. In v12 it pulled a mailbox that no
  longer existed.
- The code and config at the end of the series are identical to
  v12's. Only spec.org, README.org, and lab-claude differ.
